  "term": "IT",
  "definition": "IT refers to giving a drug directly into the cerebrospinal fluid within the spinal subarachnoid space, including into the brain’s ventricles. This route is used to bypass the blood-brain barrier and produce rapid local effects in the meninges or along the cerebrospinal axis.",
